WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:11.100
Gasoline vapor is heavier than air, so it flows downhill and collects in the bilge and low compartments, where a single spark from a switch, pump or starter can ignite it.

2
00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:18.575
A surprisingly small amount of vaporized gasoline can produce an explosion strong enough to destroy a boat.

3
00:00:18.825 --> 00:00:21.200
Propane behaves the same way.

4
00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:30.825
Diesel fuel is much less volatile and much harder to ignite, which is one reason most commercial boats run diesel, but it still burns once lit.

5
00:00:31.075 --> 00:00:35.200
Most boat explosions happen during or just after fueling.
